adr: 0230
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: kind-exhaustive
why: A condition is one expression however it is spelled, so the collector walks through the boolean operators: `if (e^.kind = nkStr) and IsChar(t)` holds a tag test and `if (a^.kind = nkVar) or (a^.kind = nkField)` holds two. Not walking them loses every test that is not the whole condition -- which is most of them in this compiler, EmitString's arms testing a node's kind and its type in one condition being the case ADR-0220 was about.
--- old
      if (cond^.bnOp = opAnd) or (cond^.bnOp = opOr) or
         (cond^.bnOp = opAndThen) or (cond^.bnOp = opOrElse) then begin
--- new
      if false then begin
